# The page and its code must never be served from cache without revalidating.
# Versioned query strings were worse than useless here: a browser holding an old
# index.html keeps requesting the old app.js?v=N URL, which it also has cached, so it
# never sees a new build at all. Same URL every time plus no-cache fixes that.
/*
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/index.html
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/app.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/style.css
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/data/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600
